    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, keeping the original signature. Money is computed in `Decimal`, with validation raising `ValueError` for an unknown region or category, a non-integer or bool `qty` below 1, a negative `unit_price` or `credit`, and a `discount_pct` outside 0–100. Each line's net applies its own discount, then the 5% bulk discount (standard category, qty ≥ 10) multiplied on top, and is rounded half-up to cents. Line tax is rounded per line from the rate table, and totals, credit application and `tax_by_rate` (including zero rates present on a line) are derived from those rounded values. I wrote 38 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py` covering each rule, the rounding edge cases (for example 0.095 → 0.10 and a 0.005 tax per line), the stacking of discounts, credit partial and full, empty input, and every error path. `python -m pytest -q tests` reports 38 passed. I did not measure line coverage directly, since the only permitted shell command was the test run; every branch in `solution.py` is exercised by the tests as I read them, so the 90% gate should pass, but that is unverified.",
